Package: MMAPPR2
Title: Mutation Mapping Analysis Pipeline for Pooled RNA-Seq
Version: 0.99.24.9009
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kyle", "Johnsen", email = "kjohnsen@byu.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Nathaniel", "Jenkins", role = "aut"),
    person("Jonathon", "Hill", email = "jhill@byu.edu", role = "cre"))
Description: Maps candidate causal loci from pooled F2 RNA-seq in forward
    genetic screens. The pipeline compares mutant and phenotypically wild-type
    pools using per-position nucleotide-frequency Euclidean distance, smooths
    the linkage signal with LOESS, refines linked intervals by marker
    resampling, calls high-frequency candidate SNVs in mutant reads, reports
    wild-type allele support, predicts coding consequences locally, and writes
    diagnostic plots and candidate tables. The implementation includes robust
    input validation, reproducible peak refinement, RNA-seq-aware pileup
    handling, and regression-tested analysis helpers.
